  "note": "This sheet is RGB with no alpha channel, so it slices to one fused piece. That piece has been cut on its stated 10x10 grid, so the entries below are its cells in reading order - left to right, then top to bottom - one cell each and none of them annotated yet. Cut once, then annotate: slicing finds the plate as one fused piece again, so re-slicing has nothing to add. 1254x1254 at 10x10. It already ships as a hand-written tileset built by art-source/tilesets/normalize_tilesets.py. Exporting over it would rewrite the ids and coordinates that GenMappingRegistry references, so treat this as a sheet to inspect or adopt deliberately, not to re-export casually. Its 3x3 wall and floor patches are what block grouping was built for: urban.wall is a wall-3x3 at origin (3,0), urban.floor a floor-3x3 at (0,0). urban.wall is assigned and was checked against the art before it was kept: corner studs sit on the outer corners, each edge cell carries its face slit on the side the slot names as exterior, and the enclosed centre is blank because the 0x060A10 fill is what that case is for. urban.floor is declared but still unassigned.",
